! Test 22: Water dimer wB97X-D / 6-31G*  [the CHG dispersion tail]
! The -D tail of wB97X-D is the CHG-damped C6/R^6 term (Chai &
! Head-Gordon, PCCP 10, 6615 (2008)) over the D2 parameter set
! (Grimme, JCC 27, 1787 (2006), Table 1), reimplemented cleanly in
! v1.13.1.  Anchors (this implementation, CODATA-2018 conversion):
!     Dispersion (CHG):  -0.000823305033
!     full gradient gX(O1) = 0.00460856 Ha/bohr (%job gradient),
!     FD of the total energy: 0.00460891 (h = 1e-3 bohr).
! The previous (LGPL) implementation gives -0.000823305044; the
! 1.1e-11 residual is the CODATA revision of the J nm^6/mol -> au
! conversion factor, documented in BENCHMARK_NOTES_v1.13.1.md.
%method     WB97X-D
%basis      6-31gd
%job        energy
%grid       3
*geometry angstrom
O   -1.551007  -0.114520   0.000000
H   -1.934259   0.762503   0.000000
H   -0.599677   0.040712   0.000000
O    1.350625   0.111469   0.000000
H    1.680398  -0.373741  -0.758561
H    1.680398  -0.373741   0.758561
*end
